\begin{abstract}
The rapid expansion of edge-computing platforms has created a pressing need for energy-efficient neural network inference, with existing quantization and compression techniques compromising model accuracy or demanding extensive hardware support, limiting their deployment on resource-constrained devices. To address this challenge, we introduce a mixed-precision quantization framework that jointly optimizes layer-wise bit-widths and hardware-aware scaling factors via a differentiable search, representing a novel synergy between automated search and hardware-aware optimization. This approach enables the deployment of state-of-the-art vision models on micro-controllers, opening new opportunities for on-device AI in real-world applications. Experiments on benchmark datasets show significant reductions in inference energy with minimal loss in model accuracy, demonstrating the effectiveness of the proposed framework in achieving a balance between energy efficiency and model performance, and highlighting its potential to enable widespread adoption of AI-powered technologies in resource-constrained environments.
\end{abstract}